{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed","id":855598,"title":"Advanced armor in 20th ed.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T02:58:40-07:00","id":855598,"title":"Advanced armor in 20th ed.","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I don't know in which subforum I should post this, so I leave this here.<br /> <br /> I'm storytelling a crossover chronicle, based on the 20th anniversary rules of Mages and Werewolves. The main location is Hong Kong, so there are a lot of eastern critters of 2nd edition, like Kuei-Jin or Hsien.<br /> <br /> And after the PCs had met armored human guards, they got interested in upgrading their own armor vests. The default Kevlar vest in M20 gives 3 armor and -1 penalty, but nobody likes penalties, so I get questions &quot;How to acquire an armor with stats like 3/0?&quot;. And I don't know the answer. I presume that there is a way to a mage with Matter or a Sorcerer with Enchantment to create such an item, but maybe somebody has guidelines on that?<br /> <br /> Do you know a way to improve an existing armor or to create a special one? All ways are welcome, especially M20 and W20-oriented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:28:39-07:00","id":855632,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're using Mage then yeah, there are LOADS of ways to get Armour without penalty. Matter for example and Forces with a little bit of Prime you can turn a T-shirt into an item that deflects bullets or stops them dead as a Rote (or you can even make a minor wonder). For Werewolf then it's also moderately simple to craft up some Talen or Fetish armour or even use the Rite of Awakening a tactical vest to improve it's performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:58:58-07:00","id":855638,"title":"","content":"But how exactly? I love the game, but all we know that some mechanical moments are covered with mystery. Let's assume we are going to create such an armor vest in W20. What spirits and what difficulties, and how many successes do we need in order to gain what we want? I can't estimate by myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:06:40-07:00","id":855673,"title":"","content":"Well what spirits do you think would offer protection? Armadillo?, tortoise?, a rock spirit? What kinda cimmerage would they want in return? <br /> <br /> The rite of the fetish is on page 213 in W20. You can also find a lot more about them in hammer and klaive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:53:11-07:00","id":855696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=855632#post855632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you're using Mage then yeah, there are LOADS of ways to get Armour without penalty. Matter for example and Forces with a little bit of Prime you can turn a T-shirt into an item that deflects bullets or stops them dead as a Rote (or you can even make a minor wonder). For Werewolf then it's also moderately simple to craft up some Talen or Fetish armour or even use the Rite of Awakening a tactical vest to improve it's performance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening the spirit of a tactical vest allows you to talk with it. That's about it. Fetish armor proper, meanwhile, is at least level 3, and some ways of making protective fetishes have been outright lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:01:48-07:00","id":855759,"title":"","content":"Mages can easily use Matter 2 to make any armor lighter and harder. Ask your ST how much he will allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:19:47-07:00","id":855997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=855696#post855696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awakening the spirit of a tactical vest allows you to talk with it. That's about it. Fetish armor proper, meanwhile, is at least level 3, and some ways of making protective fetishes have been outright lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing in the rules, but I imagine with a bit of chiminage your talking armor might be cajoled into giving you superior protection, at least in the umbra.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of the talking medic armor from Fallout 3... BE A SOLDIER, NOT A CIVVY. Have some juice and suck it up! *auto-injects dose of morphine*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:20:47-07:00","id":856171,"title":"","content":"Yeah, awakened armour definitely NOT a fetish nor a talen. But could arguably negate the 1 point of penalty as it co-operates with its wearer. Of course you could also use the Rite of Binding or the Rite of Fetish Creation to make a One Shot or Permenant special armour. Doesn't have to be a Level 3 Fetish either, heck 2pts of Cyberfetish Armour was only a Level 1 Fetish in Book of Weaver. Level 3 Fetish armour would be something more impressive. As for the Rules look at some of the Fetishes already in the book (Hammer and Klaive also helps, but just look at what things can do in the core book or indeed any supplement from the series) the rules for the Rite of Binding, Rite of Fetish Creation etc are all in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:07:00-07:00","id":856448,"title":"","content":"Also, think about non-supernatural ways to get this. Kevlar is not new tech. Companies are constantly developing new synthetic fibers, so you can reasonably assume that there are slightly more advanced armors available as prototypes or limited runs than you can buy off-the-shelf. In other words - 3/-1 to 3/0 isn't that big a deal, so have them raid a personal armor lab in Hong Kong and make the vests incredibly difficult to replace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T15:14:04-07:00","id":856741,"title":"","content":"werewolves can just make jewelry fetishes of protection.<br /> <br /> physical armour of the advanced sort is cool and all, but i think that, unless they're glass walkers, they're going to get an honour loss<br /> <br /> also, super fantastic armour might not work with shifting, because the magic that makes it awesome armour stops it from taking too kindly to expanding and disapearing. yeah, put a player in a technocracy exosuit, but make everyone wince when he goes crinos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:35:48-07:00","id":856795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=856741#post856741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolves can just make jewelry fetishes of protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite so easily. A lot of them require some specifics that might be lost, like the Croatan turtle amulets. Quite explicitly, no one remembers how to make that type of fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> physical armour of the advanced sort is cool and all, but i think that, unless they're glass walkers, they're going to get an honour loss<br /> <br /> also, super fantastic armour might not work with shifting, because the magic that makes it awesome armour stops it from taking too kindly to expanding and disapearing. yeah, put a player in a technocracy exosuit, but make everyone wince when he goes crinos. </div> </div> </div>Fetish armor is automatically dedicated, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:06:29-07:00","id":856805,"title":"","content":"The get of fenrir get a pretty hefty armour fetish. Sure, it doesn't work on the guy who's fighting you honourably, but it's nothing to be scoffed at. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the most fantastic armours tend to be devices (or the non-tech equivelent. Was it talismans?), not fetishes. Not sure if you can turn a device into a fetish but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:48:09-07:00","id":856831,"title":"","content":"I'd replace the steel plate in a tactical vest with Titanium. It would be expensive as all hell but it would be easily dooable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:41:23-07:00","id":857294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=856805#post856805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The get of fenrir get a pretty hefty armour fetish. Sure, it doesn't work on the guy who's fighting you honourably, but it's nothing to be scoffed at.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's as high as you go before getting into legendary fetishes, so not exactly very widespread. Making one requires convincing a powerful spirit and making a damned impressive physical vessel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the most fantastic armours tend to be devices (or the non-tech equivelent. Was it talismans?), not fetishes. Not sure if you can turn a device into a fetish but... </div> </div> </div> Not in general. There are some guidelines for wetware in Book of the Weaver, but that's really specific for wetware, like &quot;the bonuses for Fetish cyberlimbs are halves, and changers can only get fetish cyberlimbs, not regular Device-based ones.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:18:12-07:00","id":857356,"title":"","content":"This is of course without things like the Gifts of Luna's Armour, Steel Fur and I'm sure there's a third armour flavoured low to mid ranked gift. Plenty of tribes have some form of &quot;armour&quot; fetishes and the not limit on Fetish creation s between payer imagination and ST allowances. Extra Soak of 3 points is probably something not that hard to obtain. I seem to recall there being some Woad Talens out there for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:11:35-07:00","id":859010,"title":"","content":"oh, garou soak can be downright rediculous<br /> 2Luna's armour<br /> 2Troll skin (GF) <br /> 2Steel fur (GW) (also note that having cockroach makes the roll really easy. from 7 to 5)<br /> 2 wyrm hide one which is kinda garbage but not too bad. maximum of 3 points of damage, treat lethal as bashing (which is great for rokea, but nothing else) Not worth dancing the spiral for.<br /> <br /> There's also steel blowfish, which is Steel fur but your overall soak tripples and you can't do anything. You're just a metal ball of fur.<br /> <br /> Also you can increase your stamina.<br /> 4 Hero's stand. (willpower difficulty 8, 1 in EACH physical per success) also nobody get's back attack on you, but you stand still.<br /> 5 Endurance of hiemdall. When you're just having a laugh and want to <i>double</i> your stamina. Obviously, this makes rolls for the armour gifts really something special<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a bunch of really cool fera ones.<br /> Khan- skin of Jade- spend a willpower, two soak. Instant armour.<br /> The Rokea had a few cool things. They had trollskin, but also a bunch of other armour related ones.<br /> <br /> In revised, the Fianna had this fun one where they'd have each alternating hit that wasn't silver heal them rather than hurt them.<br /> <br /> There's also a gift that gives you two soak dice against manufactured weapons not made of silver (IE guns) but it's not really worth it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:00:02-07:00","id":859043,"title":"","content":"one point? I Think a CWOD 20 Equilivent to &quot;Armory&quot; Would be in order, for things like this and tracking devices Vehicles etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T13:31:20-07:00","id":859222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=859010#post859010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, garou soak can be downright rediculous<br /> 2Luna's armour<br /> 2Troll skin (GF)<br /> 2Steel fur (GW) (also note that having cockroach makes the roll really easy. from 7 to 5)<br /> 2 wyrm hide one which is kinda garbage but not too bad. maximum of 3 points of damage, treat lethal as bashing (which is great for rokea, but nothing else) Not worth dancing the spiral for.<br /> <br /> There's also steel blowfish, which is Steel fur but your overall soak tripples and you can't do anything. You're just a metal ball of fur.<br /> <br /> Also you can increase your stamina.<br /> 4 Hero's stand. (willpower difficulty 8, 1 in EACH physical per success) also nobody get's back attack on you, but you stand still.<br /> 5 Endurance of hiemdall. When you're just having a laugh and want to <i>double</i> your stamina. Obviously, this makes rolls for the armour gifts really something special<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a bunch of really cool fera ones.<br /> Khan- skin of Jade- spend a willpower, two soak. Instant armour.<br /> The Rokea had a few cool things. They had trollskin, but also a bunch of other armour related ones.<br /> <br /> In revised, the Fianna had this fun one where they'd have each alternating hit that wasn't silver heal them rather than hurt them.<br /> <br /> There's also a gift that gives you two soak dice against manufactured weapons not made of silver (IE guns) but it's not really worth it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise those gifts don't stack and that their activation rolls are based of your basic stamina?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:02:41-07:00","id":859242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=859222#post859222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise those gifts don't stack and that their activation rolls are based of your basic stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>could i have a source on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T14:34:45-07:00","id":859254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=859242#post859242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could i have a source on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Common sense? Decades of running this thing?<br /> Or do you honestly believe the system where the damage caps out around 15-20 dice intends for you to soak with 40-50 dice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:07:34-07:00","id":859277,"title":"","content":"damage dice doesn't cap out at 15-20 dice, there are plenty of 'double damage' gifts/fetishes and opportunities with low-to hit difficulties. Plus silver usually works pretty damn good. So yes, I damnwell do. The game doesn't work well with a lot of nice, but that's the way the system is, and it works, even if a bit clunky. <br /> <br /> That, and we've got some odd choices- Why would you ever use Trollskin when Luna's armour is simply better in every way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T15:31:33-07:00","id":859292,"title":"","content":"You should look how those things interact with the system and what kind of limitations they put on you.<br /> (hint: note their costs and remember certain limitations of the Shifter resource expenditures)<br /> <br /> Trollskin is more efficient for soaking - every Garou will have Primal Urge (a talent), not every Garou will have Survival (a skill). It's also cheaper and narrativley easier to get then Luna's Armor for the tribe whose gift it actually is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T17:23:24-07:00","id":859335,"title":"","content":"It's relatively easy to pick up Two of the Three of Luna's Armour + either Troll Skin or Steel Fur (as Flea gives out Luna's Armour and then if your a GF or GW you can get the other) but I see nowhere that they wouldn't stack. Thematically and Logically it's fine, one does fur, one does flesh and one is an armour of light (briefly visible though it may be). There's also nothing anywhere about using &quot;base&quot; stats when rolling for gifts, you're stats in a given form are as they are, if a gift or totem boosts them then they are what they are too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T22:22:54-07:00","id":859467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855598-advanced-armor-in-20th-ed?p=859335#post859335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's relatively easy to pick up Two of the Three of Luna's Armour + either Troll Skin or Steel Fur (as Flea gives out Luna's Armour and then if your a GF or GW you can get the other) but I see nowhere that they wouldn't stack. Thematically and Logically it's fine, one does fur, one does flesh and one is an armour of light (briefly visible though it may be). There's also nothing anywhere about using &quot;base&quot; stats when rolling for gifts, you're stats in a given form are as they are, if a gift or totem boosts them then they are what they are too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say anything about consecutive re-activations, either. Would you allow them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T06:30:54-07:00","id":859590,"title":"","content":"Re-activations to stack the same Gift over and over? No I wouldn't because that does defy the logic of the way Gifts work of either Always On (as some are) or On/Off which is how most work. But that's very different to using Several Different Gifts to boost a certain effect (in this case Soak) especially as One effect Flesh, One effects Fur and One grants an Ephemeral Barrier and if added with something like Luna's Avenger then your Stamina goes up as well. How else do you think mid to high ranked Garou actually manage to do a chunk of the things they do? Because their Gifts give them the ability to do so and those spirit tricks when used in synergy work out really well. Now mixing the Steel Fur Gift and the Steel Fur Cyber-fetish would be a no (as in only one or the other would work) as they are not just duplicating a game effect but their narrative effect is the same, but these are few and far between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:32:52-07:00","id":859697,"title":"","content":"It is absolutley the same. Nothing in the rules stop you from activating a gift over and over again. It's about the spirit of the rules, RAI vs. RAW. And just like that - RAW, everyone can get every gift... RAI, the idea of multiple soak gifts is about flavour and allowing multiple tribes access to them at similar levels while keepin in theme. So, no, the point never was to stack all that together.<br /> <br /> Gifts are traits that allow you to embody a facet of a spirit within yourself. If you are emulating the strength of Steel with your skin, you're not turning it into deformed Troll flesh, or hardening it with Luna's light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T07:16:41-07:00","id":860286,"title":"","content":"I think we are going to disagree on this one Asmodai since there is nothing clear on RAI that says that different gifts that effect different things don't stack their mechanical benefits. One's flesh, one is fur and one is an armour of light. The odds on any PC actually having more than Two of those gifts anyway is negligable.<br /> <br /> As always Gold and Silver rules apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T17:29:39-07:00","id":861452,"title":"","content":"No, It's pretty much the way gifts work, Asmodai. You don't get to eight times your speed by activating <i>speed of thought</i> three times.<br /> <br /> If you activate luna's armour, and activate it again, you're going to spend another gnosis but your new roll will replace the old (and reset the duration) This works on a level because if you got one success and then decided that isn't good enough, you can roll again. <br /> <br /> Also, A garou not having survival? You're either having a laugh or playing the worst kind of glass walker. Then again a glass walker isn't going to be too high on primal urge, either, so...<br /> <br /> Trollskin is a tribe specific gift (held by a fera or two). Luna's armour is in-tribe for at least three different ones (and more fera) <br /> <br /> <br /> And activating these gifts... of from base stamina? Not at all, Not at all. And if you're saying the stamina increases can't be used with the armour ones then how are the Get of Fenrir still a tribe, especially with the fierce neighboring with the Black Furies and Shadow Lords? What's the point of the level 5 endurance of hiemdall when the level 2 luna's armour does things much better? Did I mention the furies? You know half their thing is having super-powerful claws, right? Do you know how suicidal you'd make<i> hero's stand?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:17:32-07:00","id":861697,"title":"","content":"I'd so love to hear how many games you've ran with multiple armor gifts and about your hands on experience with the issue. I'd also love if you'd actually note the fact that the reactivation argument is there to illustrate that just because something is not explicit in the book, doesn't meant it should be taken as a ruling on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T04:59:51-07:00","id":861746,"title":"","content":"Personally. I have run several games where characters have had Luna's Armour + Another Soak gift, mostly because the Pack had Flea as a Totem who grants Luna's Armour. The experience was that it made the Garou considerably harder to hurt, which meant that they manages to go on quests into parts of Malfeas and over very hostile umbral locations where the environment itself causes turn by turn damage. Without this ability the games wouldn't have gone to those places as surviving for a minute or so would have been more or less impossible (other pack members had to use other tricks to achieve the same ends). Challenging the pack was never an issue though, they just got to face bigger physical threats and ever greater moral and spiritual ones. Plus anything they could do a BSD could do too (oh how they HATED Mr Morden, the reoccurring SilverSpiral Ragabash). <br /> <br /> Personally I have had a single character with multiple soak gifts that combined got my soak stat in Crinos to somewhere over 20, which came in really handy as a Rank 4 Glasswalker hero facing down a Zmei type Weaver/Wyrm beastie while trying to release Turtle from within the corrupted and calcified pits of the Pattern Web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:00:49-07:00","id":861768,"title":"","content":"The first time I've had this happen was in an Egyptian game about 15 years back, and it involved the Get with Trollskin getting Luna's armor. At the time the game was winding down and the whole &quot;Wall of Soak&quot; thing was funny for the last two sessions of the game.<br /> <br /> The second time I've had this happen was in a Russian Werewolf game about 10 years back, and the problem was quite a bit different. It started with the Get pursuing Trollskin and then breaking his butt to get Luna's Armor. What happened after that was that either the whole pack had to get armor gifts, or they would die to anything that could touch the Get. Once we realised the implication and that the (already deadly) combat in Werewolf was going to spiral into insanity, we said fuck this shit, allowed one soak gift at once and were done with it. It still made the Get more durable, but we didn't start an absurd arms race over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:16:38-07:00","id":861777,"title":"","content":"Ahem... Sorry for interrupting you guys, but.. thank you. I'm reading through the Hammer and Claive now. Very useful sourcebook!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:57:34-07:00","id":861834,"title":"","content":"Granted it can happen, but Werewolf doesn't really have a Save or Die thing going on like Exalted tended to muster towards the higher end etc. I didn't need to stat anything special to physically threaten the characters (two of them in a 7 werewolf pack btw) with the double soak gifts, because there's no static results. A Str 10 juvenile ThunderWyrm has less chance of hurting a Stamina 4 (homid) +3 in Crinos +5 suxx Luna's Armour and 5 suxx Steel Fur GW Ahroun than the poor Sta 2 + 3 (Crinos) Uktena Theurge, but it's far from impossible and those impressive 17 dice can come up with 1's-5's and those average (for a crinos) 5 dice can all be 6's+. <br /> <br /> Challenges in Werewolf should never be all about damage dice, soak dice and brawn (not even for the ahroun) and if a it comes down to claw and fang against something that isn't exactly a fair fight... well tough. It's the World of Darkness and sometimes you got to face challenges at the dawn of the apocalypse that costs lives. Throw in Silver weapons and all but two or three of the soak gifts are meaningless either way, come up against a Nexus' Crawlers Break Reality charm and you'd better have surprise and a plan on your side... or you RUN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}